prompts.prompt:
Use case: ui-mockup. Create a high-fidelity, practical ShopBot desktop application design proposal, single straight-on browser-sized screen at landscape 1536x1024. Audience: a small Indian hardware shop owner at a busy counter. The goal is finishing an eight-item WhatsApp quote with two unresolved items; reduce effort, readable real working controls, no visual-only dashboard decorations. This is a UX design concept, all values illustrative.
Keep brand ShopBot blue #2563EB, white work surface, cool gray #F4F6F8 page, dark #20252B text, amber only for actual unresolved items. Clean familiar sans-serif typography, 14-16px body equivalent, generous readable controls, subtle 4px corners, minimal borders, no gradients.
Layout: slim 160px app sidebar showing ShopBot, Orders selected, Stock, Products, Conversations. Small order queue 220px wide with search and three real order entries. Remaining space is one WIDE order sheet, not a third quote sidebar. Header Order #8C1CE, Customer 2bf1c784, link Open WhatsApp chat. Small human status Needs quote. Very quiet breadcrumb Orders / #8C1CE. No horizontal multistep progress indicator.
A single calm amber message says exactly '2 items need your help'. Below it a compact eight-row table with columns Item, Quantity, Price / unit, Amount. Known products are readable text with small accurate-looking neutral hardware thumbnails, not name textboxes. Quantities editable directly and unit printed beside quantity. Known rows have no checkboxes or warnings:
1 'PVC Pipe 1 inch', quantity '2 pieces', price '₹245', amount '₹490';
2 'switch', quantity '2 pieces', price '—', amount '—', amber action 'Choose product', smaller source wording 'Customer asked: switch'. Choosing a product will supply its current verified unit and price.
3 'PTFE tape', quantity '2 rolls', price '₹35', amount '₹70';
4 'Pipe clamp', quantity '4 pieces', price '₹12', amount '₹48';
5 'M-Seal 90g', quantity '1 pack', price '₹45', amount '₹45';
6 'PVC pipe cutter', quantity '1 piece', price a clearly highlighted blank rupee input with visible label 'Enter price', amount '—';
7 'Measuring tape 5m', quantity '1 piece', price '₹95', amount '₹95';
8 'Safety gloves', quantity '1 pair', price '₹60', amount '₹60'.
Put required actions directly in their rows, not in three-dot menus. Below table a quiet link 'Original customer request'. Under it one compact bottom action strip integrated into order sheet: left 'Priced subtotal ₹808' and smaller '2 items not included'; right a secondary 'Save draft' and ONE dominant blue enabled action 'Resolve 2 items'. Show tiny note 'After these items are resolved: Send quote on WhatsApp'. No disabled primary dead end. Keep payment, packing, cancellation, reservation logic OFF this quote screen; it is the current task only. No fake stock verification or auto-guessed product choice. Use literal English labels exactly. Fit all eight rows and the action strip comfortably in the screen. No decorative headings, no giant metrics cards, no charts, no extra verification checkboxes. Make this a convincing usable shipping-quality UI mockup, not a presentation poster.
